//! task: translate
//! ask: Translate this C to Exsecutor.
//!   ```c
//!   struct Point { int32_t x; int32_t y; };
//!   struct Point origin(void) { struct Point p = {0, 0}; return p; }
//!   ```
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §6.3, §8.6
//! explain: `struct` is `structura` and is always a value type. Fields are `name: Type`. The initializer `{0, 0}` becomes a struct literal that names every field, `Punctum { x: 0, y: 0 }`, because there is no positional form and no zero-filling of omitted fields.

structura Punctum {
    x: i32
    y: i32
}

publica functio origo() -> Punctum {
    redde Punctum { x: 0, y: 0 };
}
